Description: provider-neutral Proton Secret Service adapter
 This package rebuilds Proton's Linux keyring adapter with a narrow,
 provider-neutral Secret Service compatibility patch. It honors the provider's
 default collection, safely falls back when exactly one collection is exposed,
 and retains one bounded D-Bus connection so provider authorization applies to
 the complete operation sequence. Secret traffic is pinned to the selected
 provider's unique D-Bus owner and rejected if that owner changes.
 .
 It is an unofficial downstream build. It contains no KeePassXC- or KDE-specific
 behavior and does not require GNOME Keyring.
